{"schema":"adaptive-reading-fixture-v1","run_id":"40842355344","recorded_from":"evidence/runs/40842355344","question":"Αγαθονήσι\nResearch scope: Το «Gadronise» / Γαϊδουρονήσι των πειρατικών πηγών του 17ου αιώνα: ποιο νησί είναι σήμερα;","normalized_request":{"target":"Αγαθονήσι","aliases":["Agathonisi","Γαϊδουρονήσι","Gaidouronisi","Gadronise"],"date_range":"","purpose":"Το «Gadronise» / Γαϊδουρονήσι των πειρατικών πηγών του 17ου αιώνα: ποιο νησί είναι σήμερα;"},"records":[{"evidence_id":"e-e54f3c5e020b686c3746","text":"was a x^pot' an important question for the study of Attic camps since it is used by \nboth Pausanias and Strabo of the camp of Patroklos on Patroklou Nesos. The word \nis generally taken to mean a palisade of wooden stakes, and that it often had this \nmeaning can be seen from Polybios's description of Roman soldiers carrying stakes \nwith them to form such a palisade (XVIII, 18) and from Aristophanes's joke at the \nexpense of a soldier who fell on a stake while jumping a trench (Acharncis, 1178). \nBut if this were the only sort of defense to which x°-P°t could apply, not only would \nthere be slight literary evidence in the appropriate period for the sort of camp which \nKoroni is shown by excavation to have been, but the topographical problem of Patro- \nklos's xapaJ;, so neatly settled by the rubble fortification on Gaidouronisi, would again \nbe unsolved.","similar_text_fingerprint":"b58ca97191e8e97cf8b9fe8ff62760b6ddd28919d43b94a7e62031206a316b51","years_in_scope":[1178],"date_basis":"EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH","date_evidence":null,"source_bibliography":{"creator":["James R. McCredie"],"date":["1966-01-01T00:00:00Z"],"source_type":"OCR_CONTEXT","rights":null,"date_field_meaning":"PUBLICATION_OR_CATALOGUE_METADATA_NOT_EVENT_DATE"},"uncertainties":["ORIGINAL_NOT_INSPECTED","SOURCE_GENEALOGY_PENDING","INDEPENDENCE_UNRESOLVED","ACTION_UNRESOLVED"],"occurrences":[{"lane":"travellers","url":"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C","title":"Fortified Military Camps in Attica","source_bibliography":{"creator":["James R. McCredie"],"date":["1966-01-01T00:00:00Z"],"source_type":"OCR_CONTEXT","rights":null,"date_field_meaning":"PUBLICATION_OR_CATALOGUE_METADATA_NOT_EVENT_DATE"},"source_pdf":null,"acquired_text_path":"travellers/library_acquisition/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_djvu.txt","finding_id":"finding-60b40654dd266dbada39","locator":{"url":"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C","source_file":"bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_djvu.txt","start_char":274607,"end_char":275470,"start_line":6038,"end_line":6048,"printed_page":null,"scan_indexes_0_based":[],"pdf_file":null,"pdf_reference_base":"LANE_ROOT","original_inspected":false},"source_text_sha256":"4e38679bd61083c73a7ab542c62c34030daca0382c6bc49507369495e1cbf4fe","page_boundaries":[],"reported_archival_reference":null}],"source_independence":"UNKNOWN_NOT_ESTABLISHED","sampling_features":{"strong_region_match":true,"event_and_use_match":true,"in_scope_year_fraction":1.0,"title_period_hint":true,"in_scope_century_context":false,"direct_use_vocabulary":true,"conjecture_context":false,"role":"SAMPLING_HEURISTICS_NOT_HISTORICAL_VERIFICATION"}},{"evidence_id":"e-131ad53dc7f46e476995","text":"The small island, Gaidouronisi, lying just off the west coast of Attica about three \nkilometers north of Sounion (PI. 7, a), has long been recognized as the site of the \ncamp built by Patroklos, the commander of Ptolemy IPs naval expedition to relieve \nAthens during the Chremonidean War. Wheler, who saw it from Sounion in 1676. \nremarks that it was still called Patroklea by some; his researches were, however, \nhampered, he writes, because, \" I could get no Barque to go over.\" 1 By chance E. D. \nClarke found himself on the island in late October 1802, but though of the early \ntravellers he seems to have spent the most time on the island, he confines his remarks \nto the flora and to the identification of the spot, giving no indication of antique \nremains. 1 Credit for the discovery of the fortification on Gaidouronisi apparently \nbelongs to Leake, who notes \" some remains of a Hellenic fortress on the island.\" 1 \nThe remains are indicated on the Karten von Attika* but have never been fully \ndescribed.*","similar_text_fingerprint":"34c32d9041f7c734e2f668c450177e15f55d68f46f237df49ec1f3ae7b2e6d5d","years_in_scope":[1676,1802],"date_basis":"EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH","date_evidence":null,"source_bibliography":{"creator":["James R. McCredie"],"date":["1966-01-01T00:00:00Z"],"source_type":"OCR_CONTEXT","rights":null,"date_field_meaning":"PUBLICATION_OR_CATALOGUE_METADATA_NOT_EVENT_DATE"},"uncertainties":["ORIGINAL_NOT_INSPECTED","SOURCE_GENEALOGY_PENDING","INDEPENDENCE_UNRESOLVED","MULTIPLE_DATES_REQUIRE_CLAUSE_REVIEW","ACTION_UNRESOLVED"],"occurrences":[{"lane":"travellers","url":"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C","title":"Fortified Military Camps in Attica","source_bibliography":{"creator":["James R. McCredie"],"date":["1966-01-01T00:00:00Z"],"source_type":"OCR_CONTEXT","rights":null,"date_field_meaning":"PUBLICATION_OR_CATALOGUE_METADATA_NOT_EVENT_DATE"},"source_pdf":null,"acquired_text_path":"travellers/library_acquisition/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_djvu.txt","finding_id":"finding-6327e64504e2bc92afe4","locator":{"url":"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C","source_file":"bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_bub_gb_4HMnL8yvbc4C_djvu.txt","start_char":60041,"end_char":61056,"start_line":1662,"end_line":1674,"printed_page":null,"scan_indexes_0_based":[],"pdf_file":null,"pdf_reference_base":"LANE_ROOT","original_inspected":false},"source_text_sha256":"4e38679bd61083c73a7ab542c62c34030daca0382c6bc49507369495e1cbf4fe","page_boundaries":[],"reported_archival_reference":null}],"source_independence":"UNKNOWN_NOT_ESTABLISHED","sampling_features":{"strong_region_match":true,"event_and_use_match":true,"in_scope_year_fraction":1.0,"title_period_hint":true,"in_scope_century_context":false,"dir